hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4440","A man from the tribe of Bani Aslam came to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Informed him that he had committed illegal sexual intercourse and bore witness four times against himself. Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to be stoned to death as he was a married Person. (Using translation from Bukhārī 6814)"
"4441","a woman from Juhainah came to the Messenger of Allah sand said: ""I have committed Zina."" And she was committed Zina."" And She was pregnant. He handed her over to her guardian and said: ""Look after her, and when she gave birth, he brought her to him. He ordered that her garment be wrapped around her, then he offered the funeral prayer for her. 'Umar said to him: ""Are you praying for her even though she committed Zina?"" he said: ""She has repented in a manner that, if it were to be shared among seventy of the people of Al-Madinah it would suffice them. Have you ever seen repentance better than the one who sacrificed herself for the sake of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime?"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1957)"
"4442","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered her to go and first give birth to the child in her womb. When she gave birth, she came again. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Go and nurse the child until the child is weaned. The woman did so, and then she came again. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered her to entrust her child to someone and then come. The woman did so. She came again, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked her: To whom did you entrust the child? The woman replied: I entrusted him to so-and-so. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered her to take the child from them and hand him over to the family of so-and-so. This order was given regarding some people from the Ansar. Then the woman came, and the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered her to tie her clothes firmly. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) gave the order regarding her, and she was stoned to death. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) gave her a shroud, performed her funeral prayer, and then buried her. People said: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) first had her stoned, then gave her a shroud, then performed her funeral prayer, and then buried her. When this was reported to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that people were saying this, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This woman has repented in such a way that if her repentance were distributed among seventy people of Madinah, it would be sufficient for all of them."
"4443","I have stated: Two types of rulings have been transmitted from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him); the last of them is this, and in it is evidence that the ruling of flogging for the married person has been abrogated, and stoning alone will suffice."
"4444","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a slave-woman who commits fornication, and she is not married: If she commits fornication, flog her: if she commits fornication again flog her; if only for a rope of hair (dafir). Ibn Shihab: I do not know whether he (the Prophet) said it is a third or a fourth time. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4469)"
"4445","The specific reason mentioned in this narration could be that if he drinks alcohol again, it would mean that he has not accepted the command of Allah Almighty declaring it forbidden."
"4446","“If they drink (again), then whip them. If they drink (again), then whip them. If they drink (again), then whip them. If they drink (again), then kill them.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2573)"
"4447","The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: ""If he becomes drunk, whip him; then if he becomes drunk, whip him; then if he becomes drunk, whip him."" Then he said concerning the fourth time, ""Strike his neck (i.e., kill him)."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5662)"
"4448","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had people beaten with date palm branches and shoes as punishment for drinking (alcohol). When the time of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came, he had forty lashes administered. When the time of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came and people had settled in various towns and regions, this matter was mentioned before his companions. Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) said: You should make it like the least of the prescribed punishments (i.e., give punishment accordingly)."
"4449","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) used to have the punishment for drinking alcohol carried out with date palm branches and shoes. When the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar ibn Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) began and people settled in different regions and towns, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) consulted the people regarding the punishment for drinking alcohol. Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Leader of the Believers! When a person drinks alcohol, he will utter obscene words, and when he utters obscene words, he will falsely accuse others of adultery, so we wish that you set its punishment similar to the lowest prescribed limit. (The narrator states) Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was the first to prescribe eighty lashes as the punishment for drinking alcohol."
"4450","The lightest prescribed punishment is eighty lashes. So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) had that man given eighty lashes."
"4451","""The first Li'an in Islam was when Hilal bin Umayyah accused Sharik bin As-Sahma' (of committing adultery) with his wife. He came to the Prophet and told him about that. The Prophet said: '(Bring) four witnesses, otherwise (you will feel) the Hadd punishment on your back.' And he repeated that several times. Hilal said to him: 'By Allah, O Messenger of Allah! Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, knows that I am telling the truth, and Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, will certainly reveal to you that which will spare my back from the whip.' While they were like that, the Verse of Li'an was revealed to him: 'As to those who accuse their wives.' He called Hilal and he bore witness four times by Allah that he was telling the truth, and the fifth time he invoked the curse of Allah upon him if he were lying. Then he called the woman and she bore witness four times by Allah that he was lying. When it came to the fourth or fifth time, the Messenger of Allah said: 'Stop her, for it will inevitably bring the punishment of Allah upon the liar.' She hesitated until we thought that she was going to confess, then she said: 'I will not dishonor my people today.' Then she went ahead with the oath. The Messenger of Allah said: 'Wait and see. If she produces a child who is white, with straight hair and Qadiy'a eyes, then he belongs to Hilal bin Umayyah, but if she produces a child who is dark with curly hair, of average size and with narrow calves, then he belongs to Sharik bin As-Sahma'.' She produced a child who was dark with curly hair, of average size and with narrow calves. The Messenger of Allah said: 'Had not the matter been settled by the Book of Allah, I would have punished her severely.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3469)"
"4452","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Other than the limits set by Allah, no one may be given more than ten lashes (as punishment for any offense)."
"4453","I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, ""Do not flog anyone more than ten stripes except if he is involved in a crime necessitating Allah's legal Punishment."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6850)"
"4454","When one commits fornication, one is not a believer ; when one steals, one is not a believer ; when one drinks, one is not a believer ; and repentance is placed before him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4689)"
"4455","""The hand of the thief is to be cut off for a quarter of a Dinar, or more."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4917)"
"4456","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The hand of the snatcher will not be cut off, but whoever snatches something is not from among us."" The narrator named Abu Zubair's name is Muhammad bin Tadris Makki."
"4457","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""The one who snatches, the one who seizes by force, and the one who commits treachery will not be given the punishment of cutting (the hand).\"""""
"4458","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""The person who snatches and the person who commits treachery will not be given the punishment (of cutting the hand).\"""""
"4459","The prophet ﷺ used to cut off a thief’s hand for a quarter of a dinar and upwards. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4383)"
"4460","""The hand of the thief is to be cut off for a quarter of a Dinar, or more."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4917)"
"4461","“The Prophet ﷺ cut off (the hand of a thief) for a shield worth three Dirham.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2584)"
"4462","""It has not been too long and I have not forgotten yet. Cutting off (the hand of the thief) is for one-quarter of a Dinar or more."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4927)"
"4463","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had a hand cut off for the theft of a shield; the value of that shield was three dirhams."
"4464","Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: The hand of a thief will only be cut off when he steals something worth a quarter dinar or more."
"4465","Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""The hand will be cut off only for theft of an item worth a quarter dinar or more."
"4466","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has said: “The hand is not to be cut off for stealing fruit and palm shoots.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says: In the Book, the command regarding theft is general. Allah Almighty has said: “Cut off the hands of the male thief and the female thief.” So Allah Almighty has commanded that whenever a thief commits theft, his hand should be cut off. But then the Sunnah has clarified that the hand is not to be cut off for stealing fruit and palm shoots. The hand is only to be cut off when something worth a quarter dinar is stolen. So the meaning of the command in the Book is: Cut off their hands when they steal something worth a quarter dinar or something equivalent to it, and which is other than fruit and palm shoots.)"
"4467","Some people from 'Ukl came to the Prophet [SAW] but the climate of Al-Madinah did not suit them. The Prophet [SAW] told them to go to the camels that had been given in Sadaqah and drink some of their milk and urine. They did that, then they killed their herdsman and drove off the camels. The Prophet [SAW] sent (men) after them, and they were brought to him. He had their hands and feet cut off, and their eyes gouged out, and he did not have (their wounds) cauterized, and he left them to die. Then Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, revealed: ""The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4025)"
"4468","A group of people from ʿUkl (or ʿUraina) tribe ----but I think he said that they were from ʿUkl came to Medina and (they became ill, so) the Prophet ﷺ ordered them to go to the herd of (Milch) she-camels and told them to go out and drink the camels' urine and milk (as a medicine). So they went and drank it, and when they became healthy, they killed the shepherd and drove away the camels. This news reached the Prophet ﷺ early in the morning, so he sent (some) men in their pursuit and they were captured and brought to the Prophet ﷺ before midday. He ordered to cut off their hands and legs and their eyes to be branded with heated iron pieces and they were thrown at Al-Harra, and when they asked for water to drink, they were not given water. (Abu Qilaba said, ""Those were the people who committed theft and murder and reverted to disbelief after being believers (Muslims), and fought against Allah and His Apostle""). (Using translation from Bukhārī 6805)"
"4469","Some people of ‘Ukl or ‘Urainah’ came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found Madinah unhealthy. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to go to the camels (of the sadaqah) and ordered them to drink some of their urine and milk. They went there when they became well, they killed the herdsman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and drove off the camels. The news about them reached the prophet ﷺ early in the morning. So he sent people in pursuit of them, and they were brought when they day had risen high. He ordered and their hands and feet were cut off and nails were drawn into their eyes, and they were thrown out of Harrah. They begged for water but were not supplied water. Abu Qilabah said: They were people who had stolen, killed, apostatized after their faith and fought against Allah and his Apostle ﷺ. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4364)"
"4470","A group of eighty people from 'Ukl came to the Prophet [SAW], but the climate of Al-Madinah did not suit them and they fell sick. They complained about that to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and he said: ""Why don't you go out with our herdsmen and drink the milk and urine of the camels?"" They said: ""Yes (we will do that)."" They went out and drank some of the (camels') milk and urine, and they recovered. Then they killed the herdsman of the Messenger of Allah [SAW], so he sent (men after them) and they caught them and brought them back. He had their hands and feet cut off and branded their eyes, and left them in the sun to die. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4024)"
"4471","""Some people from 'Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and the Messenger of Allah [SAW] said to them: 'Why don't you go out to our camels and stay with them and drink their milk and urine?' So they did that, and when they recovered, they went to the herdsman of the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and killed him, reverted to being disbelievers, and drove off the camels of the Prophet [SAW]. He sent (men) after them, and they were brought to him. He had their hands and feet cut off, and their eyes gouged out."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4029)"
"4472","Some people from the tribes of ʿUkl and ʿUraina came to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam and said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! We are owners of livestock and have never been farmers,"" and they found the climate of Medina unsuitable for them. So Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that they be given some camels and a shepherd, and ordered them to go out with those camels and drink their milk and urine. So they set out, but when they reached a place called Al-Harra, they reverted to disbelief after their conversion to Islam, killed the shepherd and drove away the camels. When this news reached the Prophet ﷺ he sent in their pursuit (and they were caught and brought). The Prophet ﷺ ordered that their eyes be branded with heated iron bars and their hands be cut off, and they were left at Al-Harra till they died in that state. (Using translation from Bukhārī 5727)"
"4473","I have made a vow in the name of Allah that if I find him, I will surely cut off his hand. So Sayyiduna Imran (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Do not cut off his hand, because the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) once stood among us and commanded us to give charity, and he forbade us from mutilation. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) What is meant by the forbidden mutilation is: it should not be as retribution, because in the narrations about the people of the tribe of ‘Uraina, it is mentioned that it was retribution, not mutilation."
"4474","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had needles passed through the eyes of those people because they had passed needles through the eyes of the shepherds."
"4475","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever changes his religion (i.e., the religion of Islam), kill him."
"4476","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever abandons his religion (i.e., the religion of Islam) (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) whoever turns back from his religion (i.e., the religion of Islam), then kill him, and do not inflict upon anyone the punishment which Allah, the Exalted, will inflict (the narrator says:) that is, do not punish with fire."
"4477","""A man from among the Ansar accepted Islam, then he apostatized and went back to Shirk. Then he regretted that, and sent word to his people (saying): 'Ask the Messenger of Allah [SAW], is there any repentance for me?' His people came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and said: 'So and so regrets (what he did), and he has told us to ask you if there is any repentance for him?' Then the Verses: 'How shall Allah guide a people who disbelieved after their Belief up to His saying: Verily, Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful' was revealed. So he sent word to him, and he accepted Islam."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4068)"
"4478","Why donʿt you appoint a successor? He said: If I do not do that, one who is better than me did not do it either, namely the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; if I do that, one who is better than me did it too, namely Abu Bakr. (Using translation from Aḥmad 299)"
"4479","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abdur Rahman! Do not seek a position of authority, for if it is given to you as a result of your asking, you will be left to it (on your own); but if it is given to you without your asking, you will be helped in it. And when you take an oath and then see that something else is better than it, then do what is better and offer expiation for your oath."
"4480","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: O Abdur Rahman! Do not ask for a position of authority, because if it is g"
"4481","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I and my two cousins went to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Appoint us as officials over some matter from the authority which Allah has granted you. The other person also said something similar. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: By Allah! We do not appoint to this responsibility anyone who asks for it, nor anyone who is eager for i"
"4482","""You will become keen for positions of authority, but that will become a regret and loss. What a good life they will live, but how hard it will be for them when they die."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4211)"
"4483","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Woe to government officials! Soon there will be people who will wish that they were hung by their hair on the Pleiades, but that they were not appointed as officials (in any government position)."
"4484","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Those who are just in this world will be on pulpits of light at the right side of the Most Merciful on the Day of Resurrection, and both sides of Him are right. They are those who act justly with their wives, their children, and in all matters over which they are appointed as guardians.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The words of this narration are according to the common usage of people, and the words used here are those which people use in their common language; its real meaning is not intended, because its reality cannot be comprehended. That comprehension can only be achieved through the words mentioned in this narration. The word “muqsit” means one who acts justly, and the word “qasit” means one who deviates from the right path."
"4485","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those who act justly will be on the right side of the Most Merciful, and both His sides are right. These are the people who are just in their decisions, with their families and children, and in all that they are responsible for."
"4486","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Seven people will be shaded by Allah under His shade on the day when there will be no shade except His. They are: (1) a just ruler; (2) a young man who has been brought up in the worship of Allah, (i.e. worship Allah (Alone) sincerely from his childhood), (3) a man whose heart is attached to the mosque (who offers the five compulsory congregational prayers in the mosque); (4) two persons who love each other only for Allah's sake and they meet and part in Allah's cause only; (5) a man who refuses the call of a charming woman of noble birth for an illegal sexual intercourse with her and says: I am afraid of Allah; (6) a person who practices charity so secretly that his left hand does not know what his right hand has given (i.e. nobody knows how much he has given in charity). (7) a person who remembers Allah in seclusion and his eyes get flooded with tears."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1423)"
"4487","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) sent Abu Juham bin Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) to collect Zakat. While paying Zakat, a man argued with him. Abu Juham (may Allah be pleased with him) struck him and injured him. Those people came to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Grant us retribution. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Take these things (and be content with them), but they were not satisfied with that. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Take these, these things in addition, but they were still not satisfied. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Take these, these things in addition, so they became satisfied with that. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Are you now satisfied? They replied: Yes."
"4488","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) had him removed from there, so he used to stay in the open field and would come every Friday to take food."
"4489","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Everyone of you is a guardian and everyone of you is responsible (for his wards). A ruler is a guardian and is responsible(for his subjects); a man is a guardian of his family and responsible (for them); a wife is a guardian of her husband's house and she is responsible (for it), a slave is a guardian of his master's property and is responsible (for that). Beware! All of you are guardians and are responsible (for your wards). (Using translation from Bukhārī 5188)"
"4490","The ruler is a shepherd and he will be questioned about his subjects. A man is a shepherd over the members of his household and he will be questioned about them. A woman is a shepherd over her husband's house and she will be questioned about what is under her care. A servant is a shepherd over his master's wealth and he will be questioned about his responsibility. Each of you is a shepherd and each of you will be questioned about his flock."
"4491","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Each of you is a shepherd and each of you is responsible for his flock. The amir (ruler) who is over the people is a shepherd and is responsible for his flock; a man is a shepherd in charge of the inhabitants of his household and he is responsible for his flock; a woman is a shepherdess in charge of her husband's house and children and she is responsible for them; and a man's slave is a shepherd in charge of his master's property and he is responsible for it. So each of you is a shepherd and each of you is responsible for his flock. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2928)"
"4492","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""Indeed, Allah Almighty will take account from every guardian regarding his guardianship—whether he protected it or neglected it.\"""""
"4493","Sayyiduna Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""Indeed, Allah Almighty will take account from every guardian regarding his guardianship, whether he protected it or neglected it, to the extent that He will even take account from a man regarding his household.\"""""
"4494","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When Allah has a good purpose for a ruler, He appoints for him a sincere minister who reminds him if he forgets and helps him if he remembers; but when Allah has a different purpose from that for him. He appoints for him an evil minister who does not remind him if he forgets and does not help him if he remembers. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2932)"
"4495","Ubaidullah b Ziyad visited Ma'qil b. Yasir al-Muzani in his last iliness. Ma'qil said (to him): I am narrating to you a tradition I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If I knew that I am to survive this illness. I would, not narrate it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: If God appointed anyone ruler over a people and he died while he was still treacherous to his people, God would forbid his entry into Paradise. (Using translation from Muslim 142e)"
"4496","I came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and remained with him for some time, conversing. At that time, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was observing i'tikaf in the mosque. At night, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up with me to escort me to my house. On the way, two men from the Ansar met the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). When they saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), they felt shy and turned back. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Come forward, both of you. This is Safiyyah bint Huyayy (who is my wife)."" Both of them said: ""We seek refuge with Allah and declare Allah's purity (how could we think ill of you, O Messenger of Allah)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am not saying that you have thought anything bad, but I know that Satan circulates in the veins of man (he could have put a wrong thought in your minds)."
"4497","“Take it easy, she is Safiyyah bint Huyai.” They said: “Glorious is Allah, O Messenger of Allah!” And they were very upset by that (i.e., that he thought they may have some doubts). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Satan flows through the son of Adam like blood, and I was afraid that he might cast some doubt into your hearts.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1779)"
"4498","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) distributed dates among us, so I had five or perhaps six dates from them. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah"
"4499","Sayyiduna Abyad bin Hamaal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He came to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) as part of a delegation. He requested the Prophet (peace be upon him) to grant him some land, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) granted him land at the place called \""Milh.\"" When he left, a person said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Do you know what kind of land you have given him? You have given him land where there is abundant water. The narrator says tha"
"4500","Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) married me at a time when he neither owned any land nor any slave. He only had a camel and a"
"4501","I intended to make them feel at ease."" Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to them: ""Is there anyone among you besides yourselves?"" The people replied: ""We have a nephew."" So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A people's nephew is considered part of them."
"4502","The Bedouin went back to his people and said: O people of my tribe, accept Islam, for Muhammad (peace be upon him) gives so much that there is no fear of poverty after it."
"4503","I wish to travel quickly. Whoever among you wishes to travel quickly with me, let him do so. The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) departed from there, and we departed with him until the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) reached near Madinah. He said: This (i.e., Madinah) is Taybah (i.e., pure). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) looked at Mount Uhud and said: This is Uhud, a mountain that loves us and we love it. Shall I not tell you about the best households of the Ansar? The people replied: Yes (please tell us). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The best household of the Ansar is Banu Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the household of Banu Harith, then the household of Banu Sa’idah. In fact, all the households of the Ansar are excellent."
"4504","I am not killed? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Even if you are not killed (you will still be granted Paradise). So that person set out with the letter and reached Caesar when Caesar was in Bayt al-Maqdis, and a carpet had been spread for him. No one except Caesar would walk on that carpet. That person placed the letter on the carpet and stepped aside. When Caesar reached the letter, he took it and then called his trusted confidant and had him read the letter. He replied: I have the same knowledge about this letter as you do. Then Caesar said in a loud voice: Who is the person who brought this letter? He is granted protection. So that person came forward. Caesar said: When I come, come to me. When Caesar arrived, that person came to him. Caesar ordered his doors to be closed. Then he told the announcer to proclaim: Caesar has followed Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and has abandoned Christianity. So his soldiers advanced, armed, and besieged his palace. Then Caesar said to the envoy of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): You have seen, I fear for my kingdom. Then he told the announcer to proclaim: Beware, Caesar is pleased with you; he only wanted to test you to see how firm you are in your religion. You may go back. So the people went back. Then Caesar wrote a letter to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying that he had become Muslim, and he also sent some dinars to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) read his letter, he said: The enemy of Allah has lied; he is not a Muslim, he remains upon Christianity. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) distributed those dinars."
"4505","No, by Allah, we will not give to, you what he has granted to me. The Prophet ﷺ said: Umm Aiman, let him have them and for you are such and such trees instead. But she said: By Allah, there is no god besides Him. No, never! The Prophet ﷺ continued saying: (You will get) such and such. until he had granted her ten times or nearly ten times more (than the original gift). (Using translation from Muslim 1771b)"
"4509","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ along with his Companions happened to pass by a field in which onions were sown. The people stopped there and ate out of that, but some of them did not eat. Then they (Propbet's Companions) went to him. He (first) called those who had not eaten the onions and kept the others (who had taken onions) waiting till its odour vanished. (Using translation from Muslim 566)"
"4510","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) inquired: What has it given birth to? The shepherd replied: It has given birth to a kid. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Slaughter another goat in its place. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Do not think that we have slaughtered it because of you. (The narrator states: Here the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) pronounced the word with a kasrah, not a fathah.) (The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said:) We have one hundred goats; when any one goat gives birth, we slaughter a goat in its place. The narrator states: I submitted: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! There is some defect in my wife's tongue, meaning she displays bad language. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Divorce her. He submitted: I have a long companionship with her, and I have children from her. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Advise her verbally and admonish her; perhaps she will understand. Do not beat your wife as you beat your camel. The narrator says: I submitted: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Tell me about ablution. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: When you perform ablution, do it well, and pass your fingers between each other, and rinse your nose thoroughly, except if you are fasting (then do not exaggerate)."
"4511","O my son, I have heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The worst of guardians is the cruel ruler. Beware of being one of them. Ubaidullah said (to him out of arrogance): Sit you down. You are from the chaff of the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ. A'idh said: Was there worthless chaff among them? Such worthless chaff appeared after them and among other people. (Using translation from Muslim 1830)"
"4512","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed, the world is sweet and green; whoever acquires it along with its due right, there is blessing in it for him. And sometimes a person acquires the wealth of Allah and His Messenger, and for him on the Day of Resurrection it will be Hell."
"4513","I fear most for you is that which the earth will bring forth (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) the worldly adornment."" A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Will good bring evil?"" The narrator states: Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) remained silent until we realized that revelation was being sent down upon him. He began to sweat, and his breathing became heavy. Then, when this state of his ended, he asked, ""Where is the questioner?"" He replied, ""I am here. I only intended good with this question."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Good only brings good. The spring season causes whatever it grows to kill some animals and afflict others with hardship. Only the animal that eats greenery is different, for it eats until its belly is full, then it goes out into the sun, where it defecates and urinates, then returns and eats again, then comes and lies down. Wealth is sweet and lush; whoever acquires it with its due right, there is blessing in it for him, and whoever acquires it unlawfully, there is no blessing in it for him. The example of such a person is like one who eats but is never satisfied. And the upper hand is better than the lower hand."" The narrator named Husayn bin Hasan stated: Sufyan says that A'mash had asked him about this hadith forty years earlier."
"4514","I will have nothing to do with them, and they will not be able to come to me at my Pond. And whoever does not affirm their lies and does not help them in their oppression, he will have a connection with me and I will have a connection with him, and soon he will come to me at my Pond. O Ka'b bin Ujrah! Fasting is a shield, charity erases sin, prayer is a proof (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) and a means of attaining closeness. O Ka'b bin Ujrah! People leave their homes and bargain with themselves, so some people free themselves and some sell themselves and thus enslave themselves."
"4515","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed a man from the Azd tribe called Ibn al-Utbiyya, in charge of Sadaqat to be received from Banu Sulaim. When he came (back), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him to render his account. He said: This wealth is for you (i.e. for the public treasury) and this is a gift (presented to me). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You should have remained in the house of your father and your mother, until your gift came to you if you spoke the truth; then he addressed us. He praised God and extolled Him, and afterwards said: I appoint a man from you to a responsible post sharing with him authority that God has entrusted to me, and he comes to me saying: This wealth is for you (i.e. for the public treasury) and this is a gift presented to me. Why did he not remain in the house of his father and his mother and his gift came to him, if he was truthful? By God, any one of you will not take anything from (the public funds) without any justification, but will meet his Lord carrying it on himself on the Day of judgment. I will recognise any one of you meeting Allah and carrying a growling camel, or a cow bellowing or a goat bleating. Then he raised his hands so high that whiteness of his armpits could be seen. Then he said: O my Lord, I have conveyed (Thy Commandments). The narrator says: My eyes saw (the Prophet standing in that pose) and my ears heard (what he said). (Using translation from Muslim 1832c)"
"4516","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A nation that makes a woman its ruler will never succeed."
"4517","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon Allah Almighty will support this religion through people who will have no share (in the Hereafter)."
"4518","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty will support this religion even through a wicked person (i.e., a disbeliever or a sinful person)."
"4519","I bear witness that I am indeed the servant of Allah and His Messenger."" Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) to announce among the people: ""Only a Muslim will enter Paradise, and Allah supports this religion even through a sinful person."
"4520","Anas reported Messenger of Allah ﷺ established fraternity between the Quraish and the Ansar in his house at Medina. (Using translation from Muslim 2529b)"
"4521","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) went for the Umrah of Qada (i.e., entered Makkah), Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahah (may Allah be pleased with him) was holding the stirrup of his mount and reciting these verses: ""Leave the children of the disbelievers on their way, and in the Qur'an this command has been revealed: the best killing is that which is done in His path."
"4522","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to a house during the expedition of Tabuk, where a water-skin was hanging in a corner. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked for water, so it was submitted to him: This (water-skin) is made from the hide of a dead animal. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Tanning purifies the leather."
"4523","every time it was her night for the Messenger of Allah to stay with her, he would go out at the end of the night to Al-Baqi' and say: ""As-salamu 'alaykum dara qawmin mu'minin, wa inna wa iyyakum mutawa'idun ghadan wa mutawakilun, wa inna in sha' Allahu bikum lahiqun. Allahummaghfir li ahli baqi'il gharaqad. (Peace be upon you, O abode of believing people. You and we used to remind one another about the Day of Resurrection and we are relying on one another (with regard to intercession and bearing witness). Soon we will join you, if Allah willing. O Allah, forgive the people of Baqi' Al-Charqad.)"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2039)"
"4524","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also used to preach to us at intervals, out of the concern that we might become weary."
"4525","I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say this: ""Whenever a guardian of three people will be presented before Allah Almighty, his right hand will be tied. If he has acted justly, it will be untied, and if he has acted unjustly, the hand will remain tied."
"4526","I am Abu al-Hasan. You send both of them. Then Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) lay down. When the Prophet had performed the Zuhr prayer, we came and stood by the blessed chamber of the Prophet before he arrived. When the Prophet passed by us, he took hold of our ears and said: State what is on your minds. Then the Prophet went inside the house. We also entered with him. That day, the Prophet was staying at the house of Sayyidah Zaynab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her). The narrator states: Both of us spoke to the Prophet about this matter. We said: O Messenger of Allah , we have come to you so that you may appoint us as supervisors for the collection of zakat, and that we may also receive the benefit that people receive (i.e., that we may also receive a salary). We will also pay you what people pay. The narrator says: The Prophet remained silent. The Prophet raised his blessed head and looked towards the roof of the house, until we wished that we had not spoken to him about this matter. The narrator states: From behind the curtain, Sayyidah Zaynab (may Allah be pleased with her) gestured to us not to speak to the Prophet . Then the Prophet turned towards us and said: Beware! Zakat is not appropriate for Muhammad and the family of Muhammad. This is the wealth of the people. Bring Muhammad bin Jaza’ to me; he was the supervisor of the ‘ashr (tithe) collection. And bring Abu Sufyan bin Harith to me. The narrator says: Both of those gentlemen came, so the Prophet said to Sayyiduna Mahmiya (may Allah be pleased with him): Marry this boy to your daughter. The Prophet said this regarding Sayyiduna Fadl (may Allah be pleased with him), so he married him to her. The Prophet said to Abu Sufyan bin Harith: Marry this boy to your daughter. The narrator says: So he married me to her. Then the Prophet said to Sayyiduna Mahmiya (may Allah be pleased with him): Pay the dowry for both of them from the khums."
"4527","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O mother of so-and-so, choose any place you wish, and for as long as you wish, I am with you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke privately with the woman until she fulfilled her need."
"4528","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to visit Lady Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her). She would spread a mat for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he would rest on it. That lady would collect the sweat of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and mix it into her perfume. Then she would spread the mat for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he would perform prayer on it."
"4529","The camels of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were at that time moving at the place of Dhi Qarad. I met the slave of Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him). He informed me: The camels of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) have been captured. I asked: Who has captured them? He replied: The people of the tribe of Ghatafan have captured them. Sayyiduna Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I shouted loudly, “There is danger!” My voice reached the whole of Madinah Munawwarah. Then I ran straight ahead until I reached those people. They were watering (their animals) at that time. I started shooting arrows at them. I was a very good archer. Along with this, I was also saying, “I am the son of Akwa’, and today is the day of destruction for the wicked people.” (Sayyiduna Salamah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates) Until I recovered the camels from them. I also obtained thirty cloaks from them. During this, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and other people arrived. I submitted: May my parents be sacrificed for you! I had surrounded those people at the water. They are thirsty. If you send someone after them right now (they can be captured). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O son of Akwa’, you have succeeded, so that is enough. By now, those people would have reached the tribe of Ghatafan. The narrator says: Then we set out. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made me ride behind him on his camel, until we entered Madinah Munawwarah."
"4530","The narrator states: When he came to his wife, he said: Gather together whatever you have and give it to me. I wish to buy goats from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions because they are in need of them and their wealth has been destroyed. The narrator states: This news spread in Makkah, which greatly saddened the Muslims and brought a wave of joy among the polytheists. This news also reached Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him), so he remained seated where he was and could not even stand up. The narrator named Maqsim has reported this. Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) took his son Qutham, who resembled the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) laid him down with himself, placed him on his chest, and said: ""My beloved Qutham, who resembles the dying person (i.e., the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who is the Prophet sent by that Lord who bestows blessings, no matter how much anyone dislikes it."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Then he sent his son to Sayyiduna Hajjaj bin Alat (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: May you be ruined! What news have you brought and what are you spreading? The news you have brought, Allah Almighty had not promised good in this form. So Hajjaj said to the slave of Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him): Convey my greetings to Sayyiduna Abu al-Fadl (i.e., Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him) and tell him to give me an opportunity to meet him in private at his house. He will receive such news that will make him happy. The slave of Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) came, and when he reached the door, he said: O Abu al-Fadl, accept glad tidings! So Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) became extremely happy, to the extent that he kissed him between his two eyes. He told Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) what Hajjaj had told him, so Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) set the slave free. Then Hajjaj came and informed Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) about the situation: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had conquered Khaybar, and they had obtained the spoils of war, and Allah’s share had also been set aside from their wealth, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had chosen Lady Safiyyah bint Huyayy (may Allah be pleased with her) for himself. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this woman the choice: if she wished, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would set her free and marry her, otherwise she could return to her family. So the woman chose that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) should set her free and marry her. (Hajjaj said) I have come here because of my wealth which is here. I wish to gather it and take it with me. I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for permission, so he granted me permission to say whatever I wished. You should keep this matter secret for three days, after which you may mention it as you see fit. The narrator states: His wife gathered together whatever was present, including jewelry and belongings, and handed it over to him. So he set off with that property. After three days, Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the wife of Sayyiduna Hajjaj (may Allah be pleased with him) and inquired: How is your husband? The woman told him that he had left. The woman said: O Abu al-Fadl, may Allah protect you from disgrace. The news that reached you was very hard for us. So Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Yes, may Allah protect me from disgrace, but by Allah’s grace, what we desire will happen. Hajjaj had told me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had conquered Khaybar, and Allah’s share had been set aside in Khaybar, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had chosen Lady Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) for himself. And if you wish to go to your husband, then go to him. The woman said: By Allah! This is what I thought about you, that you are telling the truth. So Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I am indeed telling the truth, and the situation is exactly as I have told you. The narrator states: Then Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) left from there and came to the gathering of the Quraysh. They were saying: O Abu al-Fadl, you have always been met with good. So Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Even now, by Allah’s grace, only good has come to me. Hajjaj told me that Allah Almighty has granted victory over Khaybar to His Messenger, and Allah’s share has been set aside in it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has chosen Lady Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) for himself. Hajjaj said to me: I should keep this matter hidden for three days. Hajjaj had come here to collect his belongings, and then he left. The narrator states: So the worry that the Muslims had regarding the polytheists, Allah Almighty removed it, and all the Muslims who were hiding in their homes came out, until they came to Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) informed them of the real situation, so the Muslims became very happy, and the grief, worry, and distress they had regarding the polytheists, Allah Almighty removed it."
"4531","I took 'Abdullah b. Abi Talha Ansari to Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the time of his birth. Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at that time wearing a woollen cloak and besmearing the camels with tar. He said: Have you got with you the dates? I said: Yes. He took hold of the dates and put them in his mouth and softened them, then opened the mouth of the infant and put that in it and the child began to lick it. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The Ansar have a liking for the dates, and he (the Holy Prophet) gave him the name of 'Abdullah. (Using translation from Muslim 2144a)"
"4532","Anas, see that nothing is given to this child until he is brought to Allah's Apostle ﷺ in the morning, so that he should chew some dates and touch his palate with it. I went to him in the morning and he was in the garden at that time having the mantle of Jauniyya over him and he was bus in cauterising (the camels) which had been brought to him (as spoils of war) in victory (over the enemy). (Using translation from Muslim 2119a)"
"4533","I brought the son of Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him), Abdullah, to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so that you may give him tahneek (chew a date and rub it on the child's palate). I found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a marking tool in his hand, and he was marking the camels of zakat with it."
"4534","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Alright. The narrator says: The next day, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to my house, and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was also with him. Both of them sought permission to enter, and I presented permission to both of them. The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not sit down; first, he inquired: Where would you like me to perform prayer in your house? I pointed to a corner of the house. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) moved forward, and we formed a row behind him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed two rak‘ahs, then we detained the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) to eat khazeerah, which we had prepared for him."
"4535","The whiteness of his stomach was covered with dust, and he (peace be upon him) was reciting this poem: “O Allah! If it were not for You, we would not have received guidance, nor given charity, nor performed prayer. So send down tranquility upon us, and make us steadfast when we meet the enemy. Indeed, those people have attacked us. If they intend to put us to trial, we will not yield to them.” The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was reciting these verses in a loud voice."
"4536","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also granted me another she-camel. I tied both of these she-camels near the door of an Ansari. I intended to load both of these she-camels with (a type of grass called) idhkhir, then sell it and prepare for the wedding feast (walima) for my marriage with Fatimah through its proceeds. There was also a man from Banu Qaynuqa with me. Sayyiduna Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him) was present in that house, and there was a slave girl singing. She was singing: ""O Hamza! Attack the excellent camels."" So Sayyiduna Hamza (may Allah be pleased with him) attacked both of them with a sword, cut off their humps, sliced their sides, and took out their livers. (The narrator states) I asked: What happened to the humps? He replied: They were all finished. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) states: When I saw all this, I was greatly distressed. I went to the service of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Sayyiduna Zaid bin Haritha (may Allah be pleased with him) was also with him. I mentioned this matter before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) set out from there, and Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) was also with him. I too walked along with them. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood by the head of Sayyiduna Hamza (may Allah be pleased with him) (the narrator is unsure about a word here). The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) expressed his displeasure at him, so Sayyiduna Hamza (may Allah be pleased with him) raised his head and said: ""Are you all not the slaves of my forefathers?"" Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) states: So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) turned back and left."
"4537","I was asleep. When I woke up, the sword was in his hand. He asked me: Who will save you from me? I replied: Allah, the Exalted. He asked again: Who will save you from me? I replied: Allah, the Exalted. So the sword fell from his hand and he sat down. Now he is sitting (here). (The narrator says) The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) did not punish him."
"4538","Grant him permission. (and also added: ) He is a bad son of his tribe or he is a bad person of his tribe. When he came in he used kind words for him. 'A'isha reported that she said: Messenger of Allah, you said about him what you had to say and then you treated him with kindness. He said: A'isha, verily in the eye of Allah, worst amongst the person in rank on the Day of Resurrection is one whom the people abandon or desert out of the fear of indecency. (Using translation from Muslim 2591a)"
"4539","A tailor invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to a meal which he had prepared. Anas said: I went along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ barley bread and soup containing pumpkin and dried sliced meat. Anas said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ going after the pumpkin round the dish, so I have always liked pumpkins since that day. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3782)"
"4540","I will throw him into that fire. The narrator states: When these people confronted the enemy, they defeated the enemy (the enemy fled). They intended to pursue the enemy, but Sayyiduna Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) stopped them. When this army returned, the people mentioned this matter before the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and complained about Sayyiduna Amr (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! I did not permit them to light a fire because the enemy would have realized their small numbers, and I did not allow them to pursue the enemy because if the enemy received reinforcements from somewhere, they would overpower them. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) praised his decision. He submitted: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Who is the most beloved to you? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Why are you asking this? He replied: So that I may also love the one whom you love. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Aisha. He asked: Among the men, who is it? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Abu Bakr."
"4541","I command you with four things and forbid you from four things. (I command you) to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, to establish prayer, to give zakat, to fast in Ramadan, and to give the fifth (khums) from the spoils of war. And I forbid you from four things: Dubba', Hantam, Muzaffat, Naqir. The people asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! What do you know about Naqir? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You hollow out the trunk of a date-palm and put dried dates or dates in it, then you pour water over it until it ferments, then when it settles, you drink it, and it may happen (after drinking it in a state of intoxication) that a person kills his cousin with his sword. The narrator says: One of those present had done this, and he says: Out of shyness before the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), I concealed this matter. The people asked: Then what do you command us, O Messenger of Allah, what should we drink? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Drink water from a leather waterskin whose mouth is tied. The people said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! There are many rats in our land; they do not leave anything made of leather intact. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Even if a rat has bitten it—he said this two or three times. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to the chief of the tribe of Abdul Qais: You have two qualities which Allah loves: forbearance and dignity."",""He replied"",""""""I command you to do four things and prohibit you from four. You are to worship Allah and associate none with Him in worship"","" establish prayer"","" give zakat"","" fast in Ramadan"","" and give one-fifth of the spoils of war. I prohibit you from four things: seeking omens by divining arrows"","" and offering a sacrifice at the places where the pre-Islamic pagans used to offer sacrifices"","" and wearing false amulets"","" and practicing divination by drawing lines in the sand."""""",""They said"",""""""O Messenger of Allah"","" what is divination by drawing lines?"""" He said"","" """"You draw lines and throw pebbles"","" and the animal that those pebbles hit shall be the one you slaughter. Then you pour water over it to make it boil. When it calms down"","" you drink from it. Perhaps one of you may strike his cousin with a sword."""""",""The Prophet then said that among the people was a man who had struck someone with a sword. The man said that he had been concealing this out of shame before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . They asked"",""""""So what do you command us to drink"","" O Messenger of Allah?"""" He replied"","" """"Drink from the water that is being poured on the she-camel having drawn three times on its mouth."""" They said"","" """"O Messenger of Allah"","" our land is infested with gerbils"","" and not a single she-camel remains with us that has anything left to pour on its mouth."""""",""He said"",""""""Even if the gerbils have eaten it"","" pour the water three times."""" Then the Prophet ﷺ  said to Ashadjj Al-Abdi Al-Qaisi"","" """"Indeed"","" you possess two qualities that Allah loves: gentleness and leniency."""""""
"4542","A man who had no other property emancipated six slaves of his at the time of the death. When the Prophet ﷺ was informed about it, he spoke severely of him. He then called them, divided them into three sections, cast lots among them, and emancipated two and kept four in slavery. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3958)"
"4543","We were sitting around the Messenger of Allah (may peace and blessings be upon him). Abu Bakr and Umar were also there among the audience. In the meanwhile the Messenger of Allah got up and left us, He delayed in coming back to us, which caused anxiety that he might be attacked by some enemy when we were not with him; so being alarmed we got up. I was the first to be alarmed. I, therefore, went out to look for the Messenger of Allah (may peace and blessings be upon him) and came to a garden belonging to the Banu an-Najjar, a section of the Ansar went round it looking for a gate but failed to find one. Seeing a rabi' (i. e. streamlet) flowing into the garden from a well outside, drew myself together, like a fox, and slinked into (the place) where God's Messenger was. He (the Holy Prophet) said: Is it Abu Huraira? I (Abu Huraira) replied: Yes, Messenger of Allah. He (the Holy Prophet) said: What is the matter with you? replied: You were amongst us but got up and went away and delayed for a time, so fearing that you might be attacked by some enemy when we were not with you, we became alarmed. I was the first to be alarmed. So when I came to this garden, I drew myself together as a fox does, and these people are following me. He addressed me as Abu Huraira and gave me his sandals and said: Take away these sandals of mine, and when you meet anyone outside this garden who testifies that there is no god but Allah, being assured of it in his heart, gladden him by announcing that he shall go to Paradise. Now the first one I met was Umar. He asked: What are these sandals, Abu Huraira? I replied: These are the sandals of the Messenger of Allah with which he has sent me to gladden anyone I meet who testifies that there is no god but Allah, being assured of it in his heart, with the announcement that he would go to Paradise. Thereupon 'Umar struck me on the breast and I fell on my back. He then said: Go back, Abu Huraira, So I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and was about to break into tears. 'Umar followed me closely and there he was behind me. The Messenger of Allah (may peace and blessings be on him) said: What is the matter with you, Abu Huraira? I said: I happened to meet 'Umar and conveyed to him the message with which you sent me. He struck me on my breast which made me fall down upon my back and ordered me to go back. Upon this the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: What prompted you to do this, 'Umar? He said: Messenger of Allah, my mother and father be sacrificed to thee, did you send Abu Huraira with your sandals to gladden anyone he met and who testified that there is no god but Allah, and being assured of it in his heart, with the tidings that he would go to Paradise? He said: Yes. Umar said: Please do it not, for I am afraid that people will trust in it alone; let them go on doing (good) deeds. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Well, let them. (Using translation from Muslim 31)"
"4544","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with this man in a corner (of the mosque) until the people (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words) or some people began to doze off. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up and performed the prayer, and the people also performed the prayer. The narrator did not mention whether those people renewed their ablution (or did not renew it)."
"4545","I gave the pledge of allegiance to Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the following: 1. offer prayers perfectly 2. pay the Zakat (obligatory charity) 3. and be sincere and true to every Muslim. (Using translation from Bukhārī 57)"
"4546","I swore allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ promising to hear and obey, and behave sincerely towards every Muslim. AbuZur'ah said: Whenever he sold and bought anything, he would say: What we took from you is dearer to us than what we gave you. So choose (as you like). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4945)"
"4547","“We gave our pledge to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, pledging to listen and obey in times of hardship and times of ease, willingly or reluctantly, and when others are shown preference over us, and that we would not dispute the order of those in charge, that we would speak the truth wherever we are, and that we would not fear the blame of anyone when acting or speaking for the sake of Allah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2866)"
"4548","Whenever we gave the Pledge of allegiance to Messenger of Allah ﷺ for to listen to and obey, he used to say to us, for as much as you can."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 7202)"
"4549","""When we gave our pledge to the Messenger of Allah to hear and obey, he would say to us: 'In as much as you can"". (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4188)"
"4550","The narrator states: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) bought that slave in exchange for two black slaves. After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not accept the pledge of allegiance from anyone until he first inquired whether he was a slave."
"4551","The narrator says: We asked Sayyiduna Ma’qil (may Allah be pleased with him): How many were you at that time? He replied: One thousand four hundred.)"
"4552","narrates: When we would pledge allegiance at the blessed hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) would instruct us: (Say this) We pledge to obey and submit according to our ability."
"4553","""I came to the Prophet with some other Ansari women to give our pledge. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we give you our pledge that we will not associate anything with Allah, we will not steal, we will not have unlawful sexual relations, we will not utter slander, fabricating from between our hands and feet, and we will not disobey you in goodness.' He said: 'As much as you can and are able.' We said: 'Allah and His Messenger are more merciful toward us. Com, let us give you our pledge, O Messenger of Allah! The Messenger of Allah said: 'I do not shake hands with women. Rather my word to a hundred women is like my word to one woman.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4181)"
"4554","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was surprised at her action, so Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said to the woman: O woman, acknowledge this matter! By Allah, we women pledge allegiance to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on this very matter. Then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took the pledge from that woman according to the command of the verse."
"4555","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the Children of Israel, prophets used to succeed one another; whenever a prophet passed away, another prophet would come after him. But there will be no prophet after me."" A man asked: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! What will happen after you?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""There will be caliphs, and there will be many (claimants to the caliphate)."" The man asked: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! What do you command us to do in that situation?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Fulfill the pledge of allegiance to the one to whom the pledge was first given; give them their due right, and for your right, Allah the Exalted will call them to account."
"4556","Whoso obeys me obeys God; and whose disobeys me disobeys God. Whoso obeys my commander obeys me, and whoso disobeys my commander disobeys me. (Using translation from Muslim 1835c)"
